ging Face PEFT/TRL.\n- [x] **[rebrand.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/rebrand.py)**: Deep rebranding engine updating `config.json`, `tokenizer_config.json`, `generation_config.json`, and official Hugging Face Model Card.\n- [x] **[merge_and_export.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/merge_and_export.py)**: Merges LoRA adapters into a standalone 16-bit model, exports GGUF (Q4_K_M/Q8_0), and pushes to `fluxnat/Fluxnat-Coder-3B`.\n- [x] **[evaluate.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/evaluate.py)**: Benchmark test suite comparing detection on vulnerable test cases vs benign code.\n\n### 2. The SmartAGENT Vulnerability Scanner (`smartagent/`)\n- [x] **[smartagent/cli.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/cli.py)**: Typer command-line application with `scan`, `train`, and `info` commands.\n- [x] **[smartagent/scanners/](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/scanners/)**:\n  - `secret_scanner.py`: AWS keys, GitHub PATs, private keys, database URLs, JWTs.\n  - `pattern_scanner.py`: SQL Injection, OS Command Injection, Deserialization, eval/exec, XSS.\n  - `dependency_scanner.py`: Direct integration with OSV.dev database for requirements.txt & package.json CVE lookups.\n  - `config_scanner.py`: Dockerfile security misconfigurations and committed `.env` files.\n- [x] **[smartagent/ai/](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/ai/)**:\n  - `judge.py`: AI Judge that sends static findings to Fluxnat Coder 3B with file context to eliminate false positives and generate drop-in code fixes.\n  - `model.py`: Model loader supporting local merged weights, Hugging Face Hub, and 4-bit BitsAndBytes quantization.\n- [x] **[smartagent/reporting/](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/reporting/)**:\n  - `scorer.py`: Computes CVSS-weighted score (0-100) and letter grades (A+ to F).\n  - `report.py`: Rich terminal dashboard, Markdown export, and JSON export.\n- [x] **[tests/test_scanners.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/tests/test_scanners.py)**: Comprehensive unit test suite.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 How to Train Fluxnat Coder 3B on Google Colab (Free T4)\n\nBecause your local GPU has 4GB VRAM (GTX 1650), training is recommended on **Google Colab's free 16GB T4 GPU**:\n\n1. Open **[Google Colab](https://colab.research.google.com)**.\n2. Click **Upload** and select [`Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb`](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb).\n3. In Colab, navigate to **Runtime > Change runtime type** and ensure **T4 GPU** is selected.\n4. Add your `HF_TOKEN` in Colab Secrets (the key icon on the left toolbar) or enter it when prompted.\n5. Click **Runtime > Run all**.\n\nThe notebook will:\n1. Install Unsloth and load `huihui-ai/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct-abliterated` in 4-bit (~2.5GB VRAM).\n2. Train with QLoRA ($r=64$, $\\alpha=128$) on cybersecurity Chain-of-Thought reasoning data.\n3. Merge adapters into a standalone 16-bit model.\n4. Deeply rebrand every config and model card into **Fluxnat Coder 3B**.\n5. Push the finished model directly to **`https://huggingface.co/fluxnat/Fluxnat-Coder-3B`**.\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 How to Run the Scanner\n\nYou can run SmartAGENT directly from the command line:\n\n### 1. View System Status\n```bash\npython -m smartagent.cli info\n```\n\n### 2. Audit Any Codebase\n```bash\npython -m smartagent.cli scan C:\\path\\to\\your\\project\n```\n\n### 3. Audit with AI Verification & Code Fix Generation\nOnce your model is trained and available:\n```bash\npython -m smartagent.cli scan C:\\path\\to\\your\\project --ai\n```\n\n### 4. Export JSON or Markdown Reports\n```bash\npython -m smartagent.cli scan . --json audit_results.json --md audit_results.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Verification Results\n\n### Unit Tests\n```\nRunning SmartAGENT unit tests...\n  [OK] test_secret_scanner_detects_aws_key passed\n  [OK] test_pattern_scanner_detects_sqli passed\n  [OK] test_pattern_scanner_detects_command_injection passed\n  [OK] test_pattern_scanner_clean_code_no_findings passed\n  [OK] test_config_scanner_dockerfile_root passed\n  [OK] test_security_scorer passed\n\n[ALL TESTS PASSED SUCCESSFULLY!]\n```\n\n### Dogfooding (SmartAGENT Scanning Itself)\n- Analyzed 22 project files.\n- Successfully caught hardcoded sample keys and vulnerable test cases in `tests/test_scanners.py` and `evaluate.py`.\n- Formatted output with Rich color badges, CWE tags, and severity calculations.\n- Cleanly exported structured JSON reports.\n","Description":"Comprehensive walkthrough for SmartAGENT and Fluxnat Coder 3B","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\k4ran\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa\\walkthrough.md","toolAction":"Creating walkthrough","toolSummary":"Create walkthrough.md"}}]}
